TruncatedContent" tabindex="-1"><div class="TruncatedContent__text TruncatedContent__text--large" tabindex="-1" data-testid="contentContainer"><span class="Formatted">The Last Queen is one of the finest works of historical fiction I have read. C.W. Gortner brings Juana of Castile—known to history as Juana la Loca—to life with remarkable depth, transforming a legendary figure into a woman whose courage, intelligence, and heartbreaking struggles feel intensely real.<br /><br />The story is both sweeping and deeply personal, blending political intrigue, betrayal, ambition, and romance into a compelling narrative that never loses its emotional core. Juana’s journey from a young princess to a queen fighting for her birthright is unforgettable. Watching those closest to her manipulate and ultimately betray her was both heartbreaking and infuriating, making her story all the more powerful.<br /><br />The historical detail is exceptional without ever becoming overwhelming. Instead, it enriches the story and immerses the reader in the royal courts of Spain and Flanders during a fascinating period of history. The audiobook is especially outstanding. The narrator delivers an emotional, nuanced performance that captures Juana’s strength, vulnerability, and determination, making an already remarkable novel even more memorable.<br /><br />This is historical fiction at its best—beautifully written, emotionally gripping, and impossible to forget. I highly recommend it to anyone who enjoys rich historical novels with compelling characters and true events brought vividly to life.<br /><br />5 Stars ⭐️⭐️⭐️⭐️⭐️</span></div><div class=""></div></div></section></section><section class="ReviewCard__tags"><ul class="CollapsableList"><span tabindex="-1"><a href="https://www.goodreads.com/review/list/104711852?shelf=historical-fiction" class="Button Button--tag Button--medium"><span class="Button__labelItem">historical-fiction</span></a></span><span tabindex="-1"></span></ul></section><foote