ke my heart what happened to her but what a strong, formidable woman! I loved this book!","rating":5,"preReleaseBookSource":null,"shelving":{"__ref":"Shelving:{\"creator\":{\"id\":\"kca://profile:goodreads/A2QTNW721AYO2Q\"},\"book\":{\"id\":\"kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v1.rampJ9NypA3J-JBXHnepCg\"}}"},"likeCount":38,"viewerHasLiked":null,"commentCount":1},"User:8789819":{"__typename":"User","legacyId":8789819,"imageUrlSquare":"https://i.gr-assets.com/images/S/compressed.photo.goodreads.com/users/1782598709i/8789819._UY200_CR50,0,200,200_.jpg","isAuthor":false,"viewerRelationshipStatus":null,"followersCount":1,"textReviewsCount":767,"name":"Myrn\u0026#x1fa76;","webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/user/show/8789819-myrn-x1fa76","contributor":null,"id":8789819},"User:kca://profile:goodreads/ACWFKZMRKAB0":{"__typename":"User","id":"kca://profile:goodreads/ACWFKZMRKAB0"},"Book:kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v1.9yD7JGv98ifh6XDH2mnHJg":{"__typename":"Book","id":"kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v1.9yD7JGv98ifh6XDH2mnHJg"},"Shelving:{\"creator\":{\"id\":\"kca://profile:goodreads/ACWFKZMRKAB0\"},\"book\":{\"id\":\"kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v1.9yD7JGv98ifh6XDH2mnHJg\"}}":{"__typename":"Shelving","creator":{"__ref":"User:kca://profile:goodreads/ACWFKZMRKAB0","id":"kca://profile:goodreads/ACWFKZMRKAB0"},"book":{"__ref":"Book:kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v1.9yD7JGv98ifh6XDH2mnHJg","id":"kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v1.9yD7JGv98ifh6XDH2mnHJg"},"shelf":{"__typename":"Shelf","name":"read","displayName":"Read","editable":false,"default":true,"actionType":"add_to_read","sortOrder":2,"webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/review/list/8789819?shelf=read"},"taggings":[{"__typename":"Tagging","tag":{"__typename":"Tag","name":"read-in-2016","webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/review/list/8789819?shelf=read-in-2016"}}],"webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/review/show/1589783167"},"Review:kca://review:goodreads/amzn1.gr.review:goodreads.v1.5fPTOojXZZ2v8tgVM_zyNw":{"__typename":"Review","id":"kca://review:goodreads/amzn1.gr.review:goodreads.v1.5fPTOojXZZ2v8tgVM_zyNw","creator":{"__ref":"User:8789819"},"recommendFor":null,"updatedAt":1726726840015,"createdAt":1458873377000,"spoilerStatus":false,"lastRevisionAt":1459299605000,"text":"The only thing I knew about Isabella of Spain was that she financed Christopher Columbus’ voyage and her daughter, Catherine, was King Henry VIII’s wife. I did not know anything about another daughter, Juana, until I read this book. That being said, Gortner wrote a different and intriguing view of Juana. He gave her power, passion, and strength in this novel since her “madness” has often been disputed. I also enjoyed learning about the time period, the monarchies, the politics and the ruthlessness of the age. Personally, it was slow in the beginning but I'm glad I stayed with it because it did pick up. This story is not about her whole life but a snippet of it. Thanks to Wikipedia and other websites, I was able to find out more information about her. ","rating":4,"preReleaseBookSource":null,"shelving":{"__ref":"Shelving:{\"creator\":{\"id\":\"kca://profile:goodreads/ACWFKZMRKAB0\"},\"book\":{\"id\":\"kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v1.9yD7JGv98ifh6XDH2mnHJg\"}}"},"likeCount":20,"viewerHasLiked":null,"commentCount":9},"User:101670021":{"__typename":"User","legacyId":101670021,"imageUrlSquare":"https://i.gr-assets.com/images/S/compressed.photo.goodreads.com/users/1740055704i/101670021._UX200_CR0,50,200,200_.jpg","isAuthor":false,"viewerRelationshipStatus":null,"followersCount":700,"textReviewsCount":925,"name":"Patricija || book.duo","webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/user/show/101670021-patricija-book-duo","contributor":null,"id":101670021},"User:kca://profile:goodreads/A299Q5N4MYJ5JG":{"__typename":"User","id":"kca://profile:goodreads/A299Q5N4MYJ5JG"},"Book:kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v1.4MAR1z8Nhk9WkHyQigiayg":{"__typename":"Book","id":"kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v1.4MAR1z8Nhk9WkHyQigiayg"},"Shelving:{\"creator\":{\"id\":\"kca://profile:goodreads/A299Q5N4MYJ5JG\"},\"book\":{\"id\":\"kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v1.4MAR1z8Nhk9WkHyQigiayg\"}}":{"__typename":"Shelving","creator":{"__ref":"User:kca://profile:goodreads/A299Q5N4MYJ5JG","id":"kca://profile:goodreads/A299Q5N4MYJ5JG"},"book":{"__ref":"Book:kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v1.4MAR1z8Nhk9WkHyQigiayg","id":"kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v1.4MAR1z8Nhk9WkHyQigiayg"},"shelf":{"__typename":"Shelf","name":"read","displayName":"Read","editable":false,"default":true,"actionType":"add_to_read","sortOrder":2,"webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/review/list/101670021?shelf=read"},"taggings":[],"webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/review/show/3308277756"},"Review:kca://review:goodreads/amzn1.gr.review:goodreads.v1.2zY3GqACDUH1paBpZYTDvA":{"__typename":"Review","id":"kca://review:goodreads/amzn1.gr.review:goodreads.v1.2zY3GqACDUH1paBpZYTDvA","creator":{"__ref":"User:101670021"},"recommendFor":null,"updatedAt":1726570708238,"createdAt":1588315747254,"spoilerStatus":false,"lastRevisionAt":1588315750041,"text":"3.75/5\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eVisi turim tokių malonumų, apie kuriuos intelektualiose (gerai, gerai, gal ir šiek tiek snobiškose) kompanijose nelabai pasigirtume. Kas Taylor Swift naują albumėlį pasileidžia, o tada pasileidžia ir plaukus, kas kur kas mieliau žiūri Netflixo vienkartines romantines komedijas, nei kad naują Almodovaro filmą. Mano malonumas toks, kurio šiaip nelabai gėdijuosi (nes šiaip truputį nesąmonė gėdytis to, kas neša džiaugsmą, taip?), bet apie kurį, kalbėdama apie savo meilę knygoms, dažniausiai turbūt neužsiminčiau. Todėl kai reikia pailsinti galvą, kai jaučiuosi truputį perdegusi, rankos pačios tiesiasi kostiuminių dramų knygų puslapiuose link. Dvaro intrigos, kovos dėl sosto, aistringos (ne)meilės, dramatiški 16a.dialogai, tragiški likimai... Taip, prašyčiau.\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e„Paskutinė karalienė“ – tariamai istorinis romanas, bet iš tiesų veikiau jau autoriaus spėliojimai, pertepti iš kažkieno laiškų ir pletkų surinkta medžiaga, pagardinti šiek tiek pritemptais ir tikriausiai neįvykusiais romanais ir neapykantomis, paremti iš tiesų egzistavusiais žmonėmis. Į tokias knygas, kaip tikriausiai ir nereikia net įspėti, verta žiūrėti atlaidžiai ir nesitikint užpildyti per istorijos pamokas pramiegotos informacijos paliktas žinių spragas. Apart gana aiškiai nupiešto tuometinės Europos valdančiųjų giminės medžio, tikriausiai Joanos Pamišėlės lūpomis pasakojamoje istorijoje tiesos nedaug, bet užtat kiek dramos – čia ir dramatiški sprendimai, ir per vienas kito galvas lipantys karūnos ištroškę ir nepilnavertiškumo komplekso kamuojantys vyrai, ir, aišku, stereotipiškai ispaniška aistra, kaitinanti kūnus ir užliejanti smegenis, prasiveržianti visokiomis nuspėjamai, tačiau vis tiek maloniai sueinančiomis dramomis, kurios šioje knygoje nesibaigia ir neleidžia atsikvėpti.\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eSkaitydama tokius romanus, vis ieškau to, kas mane taip sužavėjo Philippos Gregory „Karalienės seseryje“. Ir nors „Paskutinė karalienė“ neverta Anai Bolein net perlų vėrinio užsegti, bet viskas čia gana tvarkinga – vertimas už akių nekliūna, veikėjų daug ir atsikvėpti nėra kada, įsijauti į Joanos gyvenimą ir linki, kad jis nebūtų toks sudėtingas (nors jei nebūtų, tu čia pasičepsėdamas neskaitytum kaip griūva gyvenimai ir likimai, tai per daug gerietės vaidinti nesiimu). Knyga galėtų būti keliasdešimčia puslapių trumpesnė, bet autorius pasišovė aprėpti visą Joanos gyvenimą, o ir sakosi knygai medžiagą rinkęs šešerius metus, todėl apimtis paaiškinama, nors pabaigoje darosi kiek nuobodu. Vis dėlto, rekomenduočiau visiems, kurie tokie kaip aš – kartais nori lengvo skaitinio, bet istorijos apie realiai gyvenusius žmones yra truputį įdomesnės už įprastus cukruotus meilės romanus. Tai čia cukraus šiek tiek mažiau, labiau pritaikyta tokiems literatūrinės užuovėjos ir poilsio ieškantiems cinikams kaip aš. \u003cbr /\u003e","rating":4,"preReleaseBookSource":null,"shelving":{"__ref":"Shelving:{\"creator\":{\"id\":\"kca://profile:goodreads/A299Q5N4MYJ5JG\"},\"book\":{\"id\":\"kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v1.4MAR1z8Nhk9WkHyQigiayg\"}}"},"likeCount":19,"viewerHasLiked":null,"commentCount":0},"User:1379606":{"__typename":"User","legacyId":1379606,"imageUrlSquare":"https://i.gr-assets.com/images/S/compressed.photo.goodreads.com/users/1509483901i/1379606._UX200_CR0,33,200,200_.jpg","isAuthor":false,"viewerRelationshipStatus":null,"followersCount":25,"textReviewsCount":212,"name":"MichelleCH","webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/user/show/1379606-michellech","contributor":null,"id":1379606},"User:kca://profile:goodreads/A2FRVNPYG7NSQF":{"__typename":"User","id":"kca://profile:goodreads/A2FRVNPYG7NSQF"},"Shelving:{\"creator\":{\"id\":\"kca://profile:goodreads/A2FRVNPYG7NSQF\"},\"book\":{\"id\":\"kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v1.rampJ9NypA3J-JBXHnepCg\"}}":{"__typename":"Shelving","creator":{"__ref":"User:kca://profile:goodreads/A2FRVNPYG7NSQF","id":"kca://profile:goodreads/A2FRVNPYG7NSQF"},"book":{"__ref":"Book:kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v1.rampJ9NypA3J-JBXHnepCg","id":"kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v1.rampJ9NypA3J-JBXHnepCg"},"shelf":{"__typename":"Shelf","name":"read","displayName":"Read","editable":false,"default":true,"actionType":"add_to_read","sortOrder":2,"webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/review/list/1379606?shelf=read"},"taggings":[{"__typename":"Tagging","tag":{"__typename":"Tag","name":"european-history","webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/review/list/1379606?shelf=european-history"}}],"webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/review/show/30294379"},"Review:kca://review:goodreads/amzn1.gr.review:goodreads.v1.j8oR4Rx83WjAt1oLiMImKg":{"__typename":"Review","id":"kca://review:goodreads/amzn1.gr.review:goodreads.v1.j8oR4Rx83WjAt1oLiMImKg","creator":{"__ref":"User:1379606"},"recommendFor":null,"updatedAt":1758903339054,"createdAt":1218889789000,"spoilerStatus":false,"lastRevisionAt":1220020410000,"text":"I went back and forth on whether this was a two or three star rating for me. The beginning of the book is nicely written drawing the reader into the story as seen through the eyes of a very young Juana. The middle however started to become much too modernized for my personal taste. I felt like the author's writing was too forced and just didn't flow well. Some of the thoughts attributed to Juana were just too contrived and what I felt would have been unrealistic for a Queen of that time period.\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eAt the end of the book I once again was engaged in the story as Juana was viciously manipulated by her husband, her mother's advisors and finally by her father. The tragic end was heartbreaking. I also enjoyed the author's commentary as to what was true regarding Juana and what he had created.","rating":3,"preReleaseBookSource":null,"shelving":{"__ref":"Shelving:{\"creator\":{\"id\":\"kca://profile:goodreads/A2FRVNPYG7NSQF\"},\"book\":{\"id\":\"kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v1.rampJ9NypA3J-JBXHnepCg\"}}"},"likeCount":18,"viewerHasLiked":null,"commentCount":0},"User:632247":{"__typename":"User","legacyId":632247,"imageUrlSquare":"https://i.gr-assets.com/images/S/compressed.photo.goodreads.com/users/1321799585i/632247._UX200_CR0,33,200,200_.jpg","isAuthor":false,"viewerRelationshipStatus":null,"followersCount":1410,"textReviewsCount":2811,"name":"Chrissie","webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/user/show/632247-chrissie","contributor":null,"id":632247},"User:kca://profile:goodreads/A1EYHFEWG93R01":{"__typename":"User","id":"kca://profile:goodreads/A1EYHFEWG93R01"},"Book:kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v1.fJ6MLDclZacbZS3FjeH1hg":{"__typename":"Book","id":"kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v1.fJ6MLDclZacbZS3FjeH1hg"},"Shelving:{\"creator\":{\"id\":\"kca://profile:goodreads/A1EYHFEWG93R01\"},\"book\":{\"id\":\"kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v1.fJ6MLDclZacbZS3FjeH1hg\"}}":{"__typename":"Shelving","creator":{"__ref":"User:kca://profile:goodreads/A1EYHFEWG93R01","id":"kca://profile:goodreads/A1EYHFEWG93R01"},"book":{"__ref":"Book:kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v1.fJ6MLDclZacbZS3FjeH1hg","id":"kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v1.fJ6MLDclZacbZS3FjeH1hg"},"shelf":{"__typename":"Shelf","name":"read","displayName":"Read","editable":false,"default":true,"actionType":"add_to_read","sortOrder":2,"webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/review/list/632247?shelf=read"},"taggings":[{"__typename":"Tagging","tag":{"__typename":"Tag","name":"hf","webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/review/list/632247?shelf=hf"}},{"__typename":"Tagging","tag":{"__typename":"Tag","name":"holland","webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/review/list/632247?shelf=holland"}},{"__typename":"Tagging","tag":{"__typename":"Tag","name":"spain","webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/review/list/632247?shelf=spain"}},{"__typename":"Tagging","tag":{"__typename":"Tag","name":"religion","webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/review/list/632247?shelf=religion"}},{"__typename":"Tagging","tag":{"__typename":"Tag","name":"favorites","webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/review/list/632247?shelf=favorites"}}],"webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/review/show/26933710"},"Review:kca://review:goodreads/amzn1.gr.review:goodreads.v1.uALkg5oTofHJty9AnkthcA":{"__typename":"Review","id":"kca://review:goodreads/amzn1.gr.review:goodreads.v1.uALkg5oTofHJty9AnkthcA","creator":{"__ref":"User:632247"},"recommendFor":null,"updatedAt":1783158585100,"createdAt":1215764190000,"spoilerStatus":false,"lastRevisionAt":1245142825000,"text":"AFTER READING: Wow, another 5 star book. F-A-B-U-L-O-U-S! First let me mention that the status updates are wrong. There are 428 pages in this book! Now, I will try and summarize a teeny bit why I loved it, and let me say I am hooked, bait, line and sinker; I have to read more about the royal history. It is not fluff and swooning love affairs, and banquets and fancy clothing. At least not in this book. It is about what motivates people. All of us - both the common and the royal classes. Both today and yesterday. It is about family ties, mother/daughter relationships, the demands we place on those loved ones whom are strong versus those who are less so. It is about how men and women and how, although we are equal, perhaps do not see things the same way. Of course there are always exceptions. When one has lived in different countries, as I have, you recognize different cultural characteristics. Of course not all French are so and Belgians so, Americans so and Swedes so, but you do see some general tendencies. The same can be said about women versus men and how they look on life issues. And this book talks about Spanish versus Hapsburg cultural characteristics. I found this very relevant to life here in Belgium. I understand Belgians a teeny bit better because their history has molded who they are today. This book was terribly exciting. As it neared the end, I thought OK, now it is over and then in the second to the last chapter, wow you will be blown away! I write in my books. I wrote OMG dozens of times in just chapter 32, the second to the last chapter of the book. VERY EXCITING. This queen Juana is called Juana the Mad. You will truly understand why. One more thing, which is very important, the book ends with a clear explanation of what is fact and what is fiction. For me this is essential. This is a superb author. Thank you C W Gortner for doing this, and thank you for the map! And GooodReads, thank you for bring this book to my attention. It has opened up a whole new genre to me. I was worried that I might not appreciate the book b/c I am kind of distracted by our new puppy, Oscar. Not at all!\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eCan somebody recommend a good book about Charles V, Juana's son, head of the Holy Roman Empire? I am looking for undry nonfiction or moving but correct historical fiction.\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eBEFORE READING:Having read \u003ca href=\"https://goodreads.com/book/show/184305.Shadows_of_the_Pomegranate_Tree\" title=\"Shadows of the Pomegranate Tree by Tariq Ali\" rel=\"noopener\"\u003eShadows of the Pomegranate Tree\u003c/a\u003e by Tariq Ali a while ago, I wanted to learn more. In the book by Ali, Ferdinand and Isabella of Spain threw out the Moors and sent Columbus to America. They had a daughter named Juana, and Gortner's book is about her. Catherine of Aragon, who was the first wife of the notorious Henry VIII, is Juana's sister. Juana and her husband Philip the Fair will raise their son ro become Charles V, ruler of the Holy Roman Empire. Reading about royal European families is a totally new area for me! I hope I am not engulfed with petty descriptions of clothes and balls and all that stuff. Charles V played a significant role in Sarah Dinant's book entitled \u003ca href=\"https://goodreads.com/book/show/62212.In_the_Company_of_the_Courtesan_A_Novel\" title=\"In the Company of the Courtesan A Novel by Sarah Dunant\" rel=\"noopener\"\u003eIn the Company of the Courtesan\u003c/a\u003e, which I thoroughly enjoyed. I am relying on Gortner's good writing skills in the hope that I will be spared fluff! Cross your fingers for me; too much fluff and I might throw out all attempts to tackle European royalty.","rating":5,"preReleaseBookSource":null,"shelving":{"__ref":"Shelving:{\"creator\":{\"id\":\"kca://profile:goodreads/A1EYHFEWG93R01\"},\"book\":{\"id\":\"kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v1.fJ6MLDclZacbZS3FjeH1hg\"}}"},"likeCount":16,"viewerHasLiked":null,"commentCount":21},"User:5647191":{"__typename":"User","legacyId":5647191,"imageUrlSquare":"https://i.gr-assets.com/images/S/compressed.photo.goodreads.com/users/1603139114i/5647191._UX200_CR0,0,200,200_.jpg","isAuthor":false,"viewerRelationshipStatus":null,"followersCount":284,"textReviewsCount":660,"name":"Orsolya","webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/user/show/5647191-orsolya","contributor":null,"id":5647191},"User:kca://profile:goodreads/ABVY5QC3AOXD":{"__typename":"User","id":"kca://profile:goodreads/ABVY5QC3AOXD"},"Shelving:{\"creator\":{\"id\":\"kca://profile:goodreads/ABVY5QC3AOXD\"},\"book\":{\"id\":\"kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v1.rampJ9NypA3J-JBXHnepCg\"}}":{"__typename":"Shelving","creator":{"__ref":"User:kca://profile:goodreads/ABVY5QC3AOXD","id":"kca://profile:goodreads/ABVY5QC3AOXD"},"book":{"__ref":"Book:kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v1.rampJ9NypA3J-JBXHnepCg","id":"kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v1.rampJ9NypA3J-JBXHnepCg"},"shelf":{"__typename":"Shelf","name":"read","displayName":"Read","editable":false,"default":true,"actionType":"add_to_read","sortOrder":2,"webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/review/list/5647191?shelf=read"},"taggings":[{"__typename":"Tagging","tag":{"__typename":"Tag","name":"library","webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/review/list/5647191?shelf=library"}},{"__typename":"Tagging","tag":{"__typename":"Tag","name":"queens","webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/review/list/5647191?shelf=queens"}},{"__typename":"Tagging","tag":{"__typename":"Tag","name":"wishlist","webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/review/list/5647191?shelf=wishlist"}},{"__typename":"Tagging","tag":{"__typename":"Tag","name":"historical-fiction","webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/review/list/5647191?shelf=historical-fiction"}},{"__typename":"Tagging","tag":{"__typename":"Tag","name":"favorites","webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/review/list/5647191?shelf=favorites"}},{"__typename":"Tagging","tag":{"__typename":"Tag","name":"juana-the-mad","webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/review/list/5647191?shelf=juana-the-mad"}}],"webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/review/show/177380928"},"Review:kca://review:goodreads/amzn1.gr.review:goodreads.v1.y-ikVjki1yft9cM0vLk1jA":{"__typename":"Review","id":"kca://review:goodreads/amzn1.gr.review:goodreads.v1.y-ikVjki1yft9cM0vLk1jA","creator":{"__ref":"User:5647191"},"recommendFor":null,"updatedAt":1779627812685,"createdAt":1308284032000,"spoilerStatus":false,"lastRevisionAt":1309720886000,"text":"One word: remarkable. This describes not only \"Juana the Mad\" herself, but also C.W. Gortner's novel. In all honesty, I find Gortner to be hit-or-miss but The Last Queen is certainly a hit. \u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eIn this novel, Gortner not only grasps Juana and her life's turmoils in a smooth and entertaining way, but he also dives deeper into the emotional pool and throws elements of both female and human naturistic struggles and psychological effects into the mix. Was Juana born crazy? Was she driven to that point by her un-loving and often sociopathic husband? Those are questions which are instantly up for debate, although it is obvious that Gortner is of the view that Juana was driven to her \"maddness\" by her male counterpart. \u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eAs a female, it is nearly impossible to not feel for Juana. Her various directions of thought flows which she can't seem to control (hating her husband one second and then traveling around the countryside with his casket the next) is painful and yet so relatable. Within the context of rich, historical research, The Last Queen will slap you in the face with pure amazingness. \u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eThe coincidence between Juana and her sister Katherine of Aragon? Both were strong females born to Isabel and Ferdinand and both were unmovable creatures whose love for husbands both passionate and cruel led to the hardest parts of their lives. This can lead to a whole new debate...\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eA terrific feature of Juana, written in a sparkling way. Absolutely remarkable. ","rating":5,"preReleaseBookSource":null,"shelving":{"__ref":"Shelving:{\"creator\":{\"id\":\"kca://profile:goodreads/ABVY5QC3AOXD\"},\"book\":{\"id\":\"kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v1.rampJ9NypA3J-JBXHnepCg\"}}"},"likeCount":16,"viewerHasLiked":null,"commentCount":0},"Contributor:kca://author/amzn1.gr.author.v1.JKMYKanUXDjpw6E92qf9oA":{"__typename":"Contributor","id":"kca://author/amzn1.gr.author.v1.JKMYKanUXDjpw6E92qf9oA","works":{"__typename":"ContributorWorksConnection","totalCount":42}},"User:2232084":{"__typename":"User","legacyId":2232084,"imageUrlSquare":"https://i.gr-assets.com/images/S/compressed.photo.goodreads.com/users/1758331842i/2232084._UX200_CR0,50,200,200_.jpg","isAuthor":true,"viewerRelationshipStatus":null,"followersCount":45092,"textReviewsCount":294,"name":"Kate Quinn","webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/user/show/2232084-kate-quinn","contributor":{"__ref":"Contributor:kca://author/amzn1.gr.author.v1.JKMYKanUXDjpw6E92qf9oA"},"id":2232084},"User:kca://profile:goodreads/A1C252MD61KVRF":{"__typename":"User","id":"kca://profile:goodreads/A1C252MD61KVRF"},"Shelving:{\"creator\":{\"id\":\"kca://profile:goodreads/A1C252MD61KVRF\"},\"book\":{\"id\":\"kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v1.rampJ9NypA3J-JBXHnepCg\"}}":{"__typename":"Shelving","creator":{"__ref":"User:kca://profile:goodreads/A1C252MD61KVRF","id":"kca://profile:goodreads/A1C252MD61KVRF"},"book":{"__ref":"Book:kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v1.rampJ9NypA3J-JBXHnepCg","id":"kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v1.rampJ9NypA3J-JBXHnepCg"},"shelf":{"__typename":"Shelf","name":"read","displayName":"Read","editable":false,"default":true,"actionType":"add_to_read","sortOrder":2,"webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/review/list/2232084?shelf=read"},"taggings":[],"webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/review/show/164608529"},"Review:kca://review:goodreads/amzn1.gr.review:goodreads.v1._Ir4S57b_vH0EqTg0vHGlA":{"__typename":"Review","id":"kca://review:goodreads/amzn1.gr.review:goodreads.v1._Ir4S57b_vH0EqTg0vHGlA","creator":{"__ref":"User:2232084"},"recommendFor":null,"updatedAt":1779599358257,"createdAt":1304183368000,"spoilerStatus":false,"lastRevisionAt":1318601824000,"text":"C.W. Gortner has one of the more interesting literary platforms I've ever seen for a historical fiction writer, particularly a male one: he takes the maligned women of history and gives them a sympathetic makeover. Not to say he merely takes a historical villainess and paints her white - he seeks merely to uncover and understand. His subject here is Juana the Mad, the famous daughter of Ferdinand and Isabella of Spain who trailed all over the nation weeping dementedly behind her husband's coffin, and was later locked up for madness. Here we see that she might have had perfectly sane reasons for her actions. We see Juana as a young princess in the shadow of her famous parents, escaping to an unexpectedly passionate marriage, fighting the decline of that marriage, forced to watch as ambitious men try to seize her children, her freedom, and her power. The march of history juxtaposes mercilessly against Juana's courageous struggles; the poor girl just can't catch even a shred of luck, and your heart will break for her as one attempt after another to free herself ends in failure. Gortner's heroine is passionate, intelligent, sometimes misguided, always gallant - and very sane. A poignant, intelligent book that I devoured in one day. ","rating":4,"preReleaseBookSource":null,"shelving":{"__ref":"Shelving:{\"creator\":{\"id\":\"kca://profile:goodreads/A1C252MD61KVRF\"},\"book\":{\"id\":\"kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v1.rampJ9NypA3J-JBXHnepCg\"}}"},"likeCount":16,"viewerHasLiked":null,"commentCount":2},"User:65105750":{"__typename":"User","legacyId":65105750,"imageUrlSquare":"https://i.gr-assets.com/images/S/compressed.photo.goodreads.com/users/1682548841i/65105750._UX200_CR0,0,200,200_.jpg","isAuthor":false,"viewerRelationshipStatus":null,"followersCount":213,"textReviewsCount":236,"name":"Raymond ","webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/user/show/65105750-raymond","contributor":null,"id":65105750},"User:kca://profile:goodreads/A282408XACOXS5":{"__typename":"User","id":"kca://profile:goodreads/A282408XACOXS5"},"Shelving:{\"creator\":{\"id\":\"kca://profile:goodreads/A282408XACOXS5\"},\"book\":{\"id\":\"kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v1.rampJ9NypA3J-JBXHnepCg\"}}":{"__typename":"Shelving","creator":{"__ref":"User:kca://profile:goodreads/A282408XACOXS5","id":"kca://profile:goodreads/A282408XACOXS5"},"book":{"__ref":"Book:kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v1.rampJ9NypA3J-JBXHnepCg","id":"kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v1.rampJ9NypA3J-JBXHnepCg"},"shelf":{"__typename":"Shelf","name"